pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test: `w` used to decrement the degree of a general PB constraint with a
% plain `-=`, so a legal degree of i64::MIN wrapped to a huge positive number and the
% weakened constraint became the empty contradiction. The formula is satisfiable.
f 2 ;
rup 2 x1 >= -9223372036854775808 ;
pol 3 x1 w ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 4 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
